  Not really. Not 'odd' at all. You misunderstood me.
  EssexMUD was and still is a text-based game. 
  IOK was the first MMORPG game that used ascii characters much like
NetHack. It took a large leap from stictly text-based Muds like
EssexMUD.
   My comment was making reference to the first MMORPG that, like
NetHack, used ascii characters not merely text.
  
  Actually, the very first MUD-like game was called Advent and was an
online adventure game from the 1970s. The first true MUD, called MUD1,
was created in 1979 by Roy Trubshaw of Essex University. Both MUD1 and
Advent were British creations. MUDs would not hit the United States
until 1988.

In 1988, the first U.S. MUD was created. It was called TinyMUD and was
invented by Jim Aspness of Carnegie Mellon University. Unlike the
earlier MUDs, it was not a combat game, but rather required solving
puzzles and exploring the game world.

